WEBVTT

00:00.632 --> 00:02.227
&lt;i>Previously on&lt;/i>
Two and a Half Men:

00:02.228 --> 00:03.849
Larry, where can
I put this poop?

00:03.850 --> 00:05.283
This is my sister Gretchen.
She just moved here.

00:05.285 --> 00:07.051
Gretchen, this is
Jeff Strongman.

00:07.053 --> 00:08.719
We have a half hour
till I have to go meet Larry.

00:08.721 --> 00:12.023
I really like Gretchen.
I'm-I'm not gonna cheat on her.

00:12.025 --> 00:13.291
Gretchen is coming over tonight.

00:13.293 --> 00:14.992
When I get back,
I don't want to see Gretchen.

00:14.994 --> 00:16.093
BARRY:
You know,

00:16.095 --> 00:17.395
if I had a place to sleep here,

00:17.397 --> 00:19.130
my apartment would be free.

00:19.132 --> 00:21.165
You had me at "free."

00:21.167 --> 00:23.267
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

00:23.269 --> 00:24.869
(phone rings)

00:24.871 --> 00:27.305
Oh, I'm sorry.
I have to take this.

00:27.307 --> 00:29.807
It's my partner from China.
No problem.

00:29.809 --> 00:31.008
Hello?

00:31.010 --> 00:34.845
Lan mao shi zai wuding shang.
Wow.

00:34.847 --> 00:37.315
No, I'm on hold.
I'm just making stuff up.

00:38.050 --> 00:39.717
(harp playing)

00:39.719 --> 00:42.887
(theme music playing)

00:44.690 --> 00:46.857
Honey, I'm home!

00:54.433 --> 00:56.934
Hi, dear.

00:59.204 --> 01:00.471
How was your
day, darling?

01:00.473 --> 01:02.540
Did you write some
new commercials?

01:02.542 --> 01:04.175
I sure did, Mother.

01:04.910 --> 01:07.111
In six months,
everyone in America

01:07.113 --> 01:09.880
will be smoking
refreshing cigarettes.

01:09.882 --> 01:11.482
Or, as I like
to call them,

01:11.484 --> 01:13.117
healthy flavor sticks.

01:13.119 --> 01:15.886
Kids, your
father's home!

01:15.888 --> 01:18.723
(children cheering)

01:18.725 --> 01:20.291
Look at all
my little Schmidts!

01:20.293 --> 01:24.228
And I pushed every one of
those Schmidts out of me.

01:24.230 --> 01:26.764
Hey, kids,
if you eat all your dinner,

01:26.766 --> 01:29.433
Daddy's gonna give
a healthy flavor stick

01:29.435 --> 01:31.936
to each and every one of you.

01:31.938 --> 01:34.138
(children cheering)

01:35.107 --> 01:37.274
Hi, Dad.

01:38.076 --> 01:40.945
I clogged
the toilet again.

01:41.747 --> 01:44.682
And I ain't cleanin' it up!

01:44.684 --> 01:47.318
Oh, Berta. Oh, Berta.
Oh, Berta.

01:47.320 --> 01:50.154
KATE:
&lt;i>Walden.&lt;/i>

01:50.156 --> 01:52.022
Walden.

01:52.024 --> 01:54.425
Walden?
Oh, s...

01:54.427 --> 01:57.061
Sorry. (clears throat)
I was daydreaming.

01:57.063 --> 02:00.097
We were married,
and we had seven kids,

02:00.099 --> 02:02.066
and they all loved cigarettes.

02:02.068 --> 02:05.536
Okay, that's the last margarita
for you.

02:05.538 --> 02:09.840
So, I have good news
and I have bad news.

02:09.842 --> 02:11.776
Oh. Is the good news
that we're gonna have sex

02:11.778 --> 02:14.912
and the bad news that we can
only do it five times?

02:14.914 --> 02:19.083
The bad news is I have to go
to San Francisco, like, now.

02:19.085 --> 02:20.151
Wow.

02:20.153 --> 02:21.118
And the good news is,

02:21.120 --> 02:22.586
once I take care
of this business,

02:22.588 --> 02:24.955
I can stay here
for a few more days.

02:24.957 --> 02:28.125
Hmm, then I can take care
of your bidness.

02:28.127 --> 02:30.127
Oh, hey, Kate.

02:31.229 --> 02:33.697
I see you're still
as beautiful as ever.

02:33.699 --> 02:34.999
Alan.

02:35.001 --> 02:38.102
I see you're still as...
here as ever.

02:38.104 --> 02:40.404
So we're both doing well.

02:40.406 --> 02:42.603
Okay, I got to go pack my stuff
so I can leave.

02:42.628 --> 02:43.141
Mmm.

02:43.142 --> 02:48.012
I'll take "phrases Alan Harper
will never say" for $500.

02:48.014 --> 02:49.280
She's leaving already?

02:49.282 --> 02:50.681
Oh, I hope she doesn't
use that bathroom.

02:50.683 --> 02:52.683
I clogged the
toilet again.

02:52.685 --> 02:54.919
No, she's only gone
for a couple days.

02:54.921 --> 02:57.221
And then I'm gonna ask her
to marry me.

02:57.223 --> 02:58.189
Wait, married?

02:58.191 --> 02:59.657
Well, isn't that
a little fast?

02:59.659 --> 03:01.225
(groans)
Walden, you're always jumping

03:01.227 --> 03:02.359
into these kind of things,

03:02.361 --> 03:03.761
and you...
You can still live here.

03:03.763 --> 03:05.563
Mazel tov!

03:05.565 --> 03:07.431
♪ Men, men, men, men,
manly men, men, men ♪

03:07.433 --> 03:08.964
♪ Ah.
♪ Men.

03:08.965 --> 03:12.965
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 11x19 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Lan Mao Shi Zai Wuding Shang&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on

03:12.966 --> 03:17.966
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>

03:17.992 --> 03:20.627
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

03:20.629 --> 03:22.662
Hey. Hi.
Hey.

03:22.664 --> 03:23.730
What you guys doing?

03:23.732 --> 03:25.332
I am taking Jenny to the movies.

03:25.334 --> 03:26.833
Okay, you're
not taking me.

03:26.835 --> 03:29.369
Taking me implies
we're going on a date.

03:29.371 --> 03:31.171
I'm a lesbian. If
anything, I'm taking you

03:31.173 --> 03:34.107
'cause you can't get into an
R-rated movie by yourself.

03:34.942 --> 03:36.943
Hey. Hold on.
Uh, before you go,

03:36.945 --> 03:38.145
which one
of these engagement rings

03:38.147 --> 03:39.346
do you think Kate would like?

03:39.348 --> 03:41.181
W... what?

03:41.183 --> 03:42.516
You're gonna ask her
to marry you?

03:42.518 --> 03:44.384
She's only been back
for one day.

03:44.386 --> 03:46.253
Yeah. She's the one.

03:46.255 --> 03:49.623
(chuckles) Do you know how rare
it is to meet the one?

03:49.625 --> 03:53.226
Let alone have it happen
every six months?

03:53.228 --> 03:54.928
No, no. This is...
this is different.

03:54.930 --> 03:58.031
I-I am... really in love
with Kate.

03:58.033 --> 03:59.699
Okay, I really love
my life-size anime doll,

03:59.701 --> 04:01.801
but it would be a little weird
if I married it.

04:02.603 --> 04:04.804
Right?

04:06.741 --> 04:10.544
Look, Walden, you're in love
with being in love.

04:10.546 --> 04:12.712
You live like you're
in a romantic comedy.

04:12.714 --> 04:15.282
You know who's gonna play you
in the movie about your life?

04:15.284 --> 04:17.250
Julia Roberts.

04:18.519 --> 04:22.822
Just... do what my dad did.
Don't buy the cow if you can get

04:22.824 --> 04:25.992
the lactating stripper to
give you the milk for free.

04:27.061 --> 04:28.795
Come on, Barry,
let's go.

04:28.797 --> 04:30.897
You know who would play me
and you in the movie?

04:30.899 --> 04:32.465
Tom Hanks and Meg Ryan.

04:32.467 --> 04:35.302
I'll be either one.

04:36.170 --> 04:38.438
(sighs)

04:40.007 --> 04:42.209
Hey, Charlie.

04:42.211 --> 04:45.312
It's me, Walden.

04:45.314 --> 04:50.817
We... never met, but I'm the guy
who took your place.

04:53.120 --> 04:56.089
Thanks for giving up your house.

04:56.091 --> 05:00.160
I guess you didn't really
give it up-- you died.

05:00.162 --> 05:04.231
You'd have to be on crack
to give up all this.

05:08.569 --> 05:10.604
Anyway, I...

05:10.606 --> 05:11.972
Is Jenny right?

05:11.974 --> 05:16.576
I mean, do I fall in love
too fast?

05:16.578 --> 05:18.378
Come on, Charlie,

05:18.380 --> 05:20.080
talk to me.

05:20.082 --> 05:22.649
At least show me a sign.

05:22.651 --> 05:24.918
(chuckles)
Yeah.

05:24.920 --> 05:26.920
That's what I thought.

05:26.922 --> 05:27.954
(knocking)
(yelps)

05:27.956 --> 05:29.389
(thunder rumbles)

05:35.763 --> 05:38.164
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

05:38.166 --> 05:40.567
Here, try my
famous guacamole.

05:40.569 --> 05:41.735
Oh, what makes it famous?

05:41.737 --> 05:42.702
I don't know. It's...

05:42.704 --> 05:44.170
really good
and everybody likes it.

05:44.172 --> 05:46.172
I didn't think
you'd actually call me on it.

05:46.174 --> 05:48.174
Do you have any
famous recipes?

05:48.176 --> 05:51.511
Well, there's the-the Strongman
family meatloaf.

05:51.513 --> 05:52.979
You'll have to make that for me.

05:52.981 --> 05:54.614
Uh, the recipe died
with my grandmother.

05:54.639 --> 05:55.216
Oh.

05:55.217 --> 05:57.217
We'd always say,
"Write it down, write it down."

05:57.219 --> 05:59.586
And she'd say...
(European accent): "Tomorrow."

05:59.588 --> 06:02.455
One day, your tomorrows
run out.

06:02.457 --> 06:04.991
Oh, Nana Strongman.
Aw.

06:04.993 --> 06:07.627
Every day, I learn something new
about my Jeff.

06:07.629 --> 06:09.362
(chuckles)
You and me both.

06:09.364 --> 06:11.598
I wish we could be
together every day.

06:11.600 --> 06:13.033
Oh, what would that be like?

06:13.035 --> 06:14.467
Well, let's put it this way:

06:14.469 --> 06:17.570
The Strongman meat
would not be loafing.

06:17.572 --> 06:18.905
Move in with me.

06:18.907 --> 06:20.240
Seriously?

06:20.242 --> 06:21.841
You make this place a home.

06:21.843 --> 06:23.877
When you're not here,
this apartment feels

06:23.879 --> 06:25.779
like it belongs
to somebody else.

06:27.448 --> 06:28.848
So what do you say?

06:28.850 --> 06:30.050
I say yes.

06:30.052 --> 06:31.818
Oh, my God, that's great!

06:31.820 --> 06:34.187
But I insist
on paying half the rent.

06:34.189 --> 06:35.388
I love you.

06:36.357 --> 06:37.724
Cash only.

06:39.226 --> 06:41.961
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

06:43.097 --> 06:44.064
Can I help you?

06:44.066 --> 06:45.532
Hey, sorry to bother you. I...

06:45.534 --> 06:47.767
I've been hiking all day, and
I saw you had a hose out here,

06:47.769 --> 06:50.070
and I was wondering if I could
fill up my water bottle.

06:50.072 --> 06:52.739
I have a hose?

06:53.574 --> 06:54.741
Yeah.

06:54.743 --> 06:56.142
Bottom of the stairs.

06:56.144 --> 06:57.477
Good for me.

06:57.479 --> 07:01.081
Uh, I... actually, I have
filtered water in the kitchen.

07:01.083 --> 07:03.483
Oh, I kind of had my heart set
on dirty hose water,

07:03.485 --> 07:05.418
but if you insist.

07:09.590 --> 07:12.726
(angelic choir singing)

07:14.462 --> 07:16.396
Should I...

07:17.131 --> 07:18.732
I'm sorry, what?

07:18.734 --> 07:20.500
(chuckles)
Sh-Should I wipe my feet?

07:20.502 --> 07:21.534
I-I don't want

07:21.536 --> 07:23.403
to track beach sand into your...

07:25.639 --> 07:27.006
...house sand?

07:27.008 --> 07:28.908
Oh, no. That's-that's not sand.

07:28.910 --> 07:31.778
That's the remains of the guy
who used to live here.

07:33.848 --> 07:35.349
You know what, maybe I'll just
use the hose outside. It's fine.

07:35.374 --> 07:36.584
No, no, no, no.

07:36.585 --> 07:38.585
No, it's not like that.
He gets spilled all the time.

07:38.587 --> 07:41.521
At this point, he's mostly lint.
I'm Walden.

07:41.523 --> 07:43.957
Vivian.

07:43.959 --> 07:45.658
That's a beautiful name.

07:45.660 --> 07:48.661
Thank you. My parents got it
from that '70s show.

07:50.264 --> 07:52.732
What was it called? &lt;i>Maude.&lt;/i>

07:52.734 --> 07:54.167
Ah.
Yeah.

07:54.169 --> 07:56.269
Wow, this is...

07:56.271 --> 07:58.805
this is quite a place.
(chuckles)

07:58.807 --> 08:00.640
Your desk is backwards.

08:00.642 --> 08:02.375
Excuse me?

08:02.377 --> 08:04.711
Well, you have this
beautiful view of the ocean,

08:04.713 --> 08:07.580
and yet your desk
is facing the wall with...

08:07.582 --> 08:10.016
a picture of the ocean on it.

08:10.018 --> 08:13.553
Yeah. It's... actually,
it's-it's the Atlantic.

08:14.355 --> 08:16.022
(chuckles)

08:20.294 --> 08:22.028
It's an inside joke.

08:23.063 --> 08:26.032
For myself.

08:26.667 --> 08:28.268
(thunder rumbles)

08:28.270 --> 08:30.470
Uh, you know what,
I better fill up and get going.

08:30.472 --> 08:32.939
But it's, like... it's really
starting to come down out there.

08:32.941 --> 08:35.275
It's just a little water.
I'm not gonna melt.

08:35.277 --> 08:38.411
It's not like I'm
the Wicked Witch of the West.

08:38.413 --> 08:40.747
I mean, you could wait it out
here if you want.

08:40.749 --> 08:42.282
We could have dinner together.

08:42.284 --> 08:44.417
I'll-I'll order delivery.

08:44.419 --> 08:45.585
Really?

08:45.587 --> 08:47.620
Wow. Uh, yeah.

08:47.622 --> 08:48.955
That'd be great.

08:48.957 --> 08:50.190
Great.
Okay.

08:50.192 --> 08:53.026
(chuckles)
Thank you.

08:53.028 --> 08:55.295
You know, I-I got to ask,
do you always invite strangers

08:55.297 --> 08:56.329
into your home?

08:56.331 --> 08:59.032
Oh, no.
Usually they invite themselves.

08:59.800 --> 09:01.401
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

09:01.403 --> 09:04.137
I am so excited to
move in with you.

09:04.139 --> 09:05.405
Hey, on top of paying
half the rent,

09:05.407 --> 09:07.240
I insist on paying
half the utilities.

09:07.242 --> 09:09.809
Thank you. By the way,
there's also a security deposit,

09:09.811 --> 09:11.444
a cleaning deposit
and the groceries

09:11.446 --> 09:14.180
you've already eaten half of.
But we'll figure that out later.

09:14.182 --> 09:16.716
We're gonna have so much fun.
(chuckles)

09:16.718 --> 09:18.751
Oh. Oh. If this is gonna get
any more physical,

09:18.753 --> 09:20.086
I got to go freshen up.

09:20.088 --> 09:21.421
You mean poop?

09:21.423 --> 09:23.456
I love you so much.

09:26.126 --> 09:28.061
Oh, hey, if, uh,
the pizza guy shows up,

09:28.063 --> 09:29.262
I don't have any money.

09:29.264 --> 09:30.730
Hey, that's my line!

09:30.732 --> 09:34.734
My wallet's on the counter.
Thanks.

09:36.504 --> 09:42.775
(slow motion):
Wait...!

09:42.777 --> 09:45.445
Who's Alan Harper?

09:45.447 --> 09:48.715
A guy who no longer has to poop.

09:49.450 --> 09:51.084
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

09:51.086 --> 09:52.886
So, what's your deal,
Walden?

09:52.888 --> 09:57.557
Good-looking guy, rich,
Malibu beach house.

09:57.559 --> 10:00.560
I bet you only date
hot actresses.

10:00.562 --> 10:03.930
God, no.
I'd never date an actress.

10:05.232 --> 10:06.499
They're all crazy.

10:06.501 --> 10:09.269
I'm sure they're not all crazy.

10:09.271 --> 10:11.671
Trust me. They are.

10:11.673 --> 10:13.506
I don't get
this whole fascination

10:13.508 --> 10:15.074
with celebrities anyway.

10:15.076 --> 10:17.710
I mean, who cares
who's dating whom

10:17.712 --> 10:19.445
or who's engaged to who

10:19.447 --> 10:24.417
or who has a sex tape
that no one will ever, ever see?

10:25.519 --> 10:27.654
I know. But I have to say

10:27.656 --> 10:30.056
I am a sucker for anything
having to do

10:30.058 --> 10:31.824
with Brangelina or Kimye.

10:31.826 --> 10:33.693
Yeah, I have no idea
what that means.

10:33.695 --> 10:36.095
I thought we were eating Kimye.

10:36.097 --> 10:38.531
What, have you been hiding under
a rock for the last few years?

10:38.533 --> 10:40.500
No, but I have climbed a few.

10:40.502 --> 10:42.335
I was a Sherpa in Nepal.

10:42.337 --> 10:43.570
Yeah.
And I...

10:43.572 --> 10:45.171
I drove cattle in Argentina.

10:45.173 --> 10:47.807
And I, uh... Oh, I used
to give safari tours in Africa.

10:47.809 --> 10:51.377
And, once, I was an assistant
manager at a Hot Dog on a Stick

10:51.379 --> 10:52.445
in Pittsburgh.

10:52.447 --> 10:53.813
I love hot dogs.

10:53.815 --> 10:55.214
(laughs)

10:55.216 --> 10:57.250
I've never even thought
about doing stuff like that.

10:57.252 --> 10:58.851
I mean, although I did

10:58.853 --> 11:02.922
once sit in the splash section
at SeaWorld without a poncho.

11:02.924 --> 11:06.192
Well, then you'd be perfect
for my next adventure.

11:06.194 --> 11:08.661
Crewing on a sailboat
to Polynesia.

11:08.663 --> 11:10.463
Wow.

11:10.465 --> 11:12.632
A sailboat to Polynesia.

11:17.805 --> 11:21.207
So what island do you
want to hit first?

11:21.209 --> 11:22.875
As long as we're together,

11:22.877 --> 11:24.811
it doesn't matter.

11:26.580 --> 11:28.982
(gasping)

11:30.417 --> 11:32.018
That was a close one.

11:32.020 --> 11:33.853
I barely caught you guys.

11:34.888 --> 11:36.222
I'm still living
with you, right?

11:36.224 --> 11:38.391
Whoa...

11:44.665 --> 11:46.599
VIVIAN (distant):
&lt;i>Walden.&lt;/i>

11:46.601 --> 11:49.068
Walden.
Huh?

11:49.070 --> 11:50.870
Which one do you want?

11:50.872 --> 11:53.039
Right now I want both.

11:53.041 --> 11:55.408
Oh, here. (laughs)

11:56.243 --> 11:58.044
Oh.

11:59.013 --> 12:02.181
"A new love awaits you."

12:03.751 --> 12:05.051
Wow.

12:06.053 --> 12:09.355
Mine says,
"Try our gluten-free wontons."

12:10.958 --> 12:12.458
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

12:12.460 --> 12:16.796
Okay, uh, you asked, uh,
"Who is Alan Harper""

12:16.798 --> 12:19.198
And you deserve
the truth.

12:19.200 --> 12:20.900
My real name is Alan Harper.

12:20.902 --> 12:23.636
I-I used to date Lyndsey,
but when she broke up with me,

12:23.638 --> 12:25.238
I wanted to meet
her new boyfriend, Larry,

12:25.240 --> 12:27.140
but I didn't want him
to know that it was me,

12:27.142 --> 12:28.508
so I created a fake persona,
Jeff Strongman,

12:28.510 --> 12:30.176
but then Larry and I
became real friends,

12:30.178 --> 12:31.911
and then you came along,
and I really liked you,

12:31.913 --> 12:33.880
and everything was perfect
until you picked up my wallet

12:33.882 --> 12:36.115
to pay for the pizza,
which reinforces my one rule:

12:36.117 --> 12:38.918
"Never offer
to pay for anything!"

12:40.120 --> 12:44.624
Wow. So nothing I know
about you is real?

12:44.626 --> 12:45.792
My-my feelings for you are real.

12:45.794 --> 12:47.560
And I was telling the truth
when I said

12:47.562 --> 12:48.861
I wanted you to live with me.

12:48.863 --> 12:50.463
What about your son?

12:50.465 --> 12:52.165
Oh, oh, that-that wasn't a lie.

12:52.167 --> 12:54.500
I have a son,
just not the guy you met.

12:54.502 --> 12:56.669
M.I.T.?

12:56.671 --> 12:57.570
L.I.E.

12:57.572 --> 12:58.938
Anything else?

12:58.940 --> 13:03.176
I take regular condoms, and I
put them in the Magnum box.

13:03.178 --> 13:06.245
Yeah, I kind of figured that.

13:07.548 --> 13:09.082
All right, good-bye, Jeff.

13:09.084 --> 13:10.616
Alan. Whatever your name is.

13:10.618 --> 13:12.385
Please, Gretchen, Gretchen,
don't go, don't go.

13:12.387 --> 13:13.820
I really do care
for you. Oh!

13:13.822 --> 13:16.255
Gretchen, come back!

13:16.257 --> 13:18.591
You have the pizza coupon!

13:18.593 --> 13:20.460
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

13:27.071 --> 13:29.239
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

13:30.541 --> 13:33.109
Wow, look at you.

13:33.111 --> 13:37.146
Now you can look at the ocean
and watch porn at the same time.

13:37.148 --> 13:40.216
Oh, I don't like looking
at naked women.

13:40.951 --> 13:42.919
That didn't
come out right.

13:42.921 --> 13:45.455
I use this computer
for work.

13:45.457 --> 13:47.624
In fact, it's what paid
for this view.

13:47.626 --> 13:49.158
This view is free.

13:49.160 --> 13:52.729
Everything you say
is like a bumper sticker.

13:54.331 --> 13:57.333
Well, I'm just gonna
keep on truckin', then!

13:57.335 --> 13:59.969
Hey, don't forget to coexist.

14:01.906 --> 14:03.473
You know, it's with all
the religious symbols?

14:03.475 --> 14:05.708
The star of David
and the fish.

14:05.710 --> 14:07.610
It's a bumper sticker.
Never mind.

14:07.612 --> 14:09.646
All right, where-where...
where you headed?

14:09.648 --> 14:11.514
Carbon Canyon tonight,
and then the...

14:11.516 --> 14:14.117
the road is open,
and so is my mind.

14:14.119 --> 14:17.687
(gasps) Ooh, that could be
a bumper sticker.

14:17.689 --> 14:20.323
Hey, uh, why don't you give me
your number?

14:20.325 --> 14:21.824
We'll have to stay in touch.

14:21.826 --> 14:24.294
I don't have a phone.

14:24.296 --> 14:26.296
That is awesome.

14:27.665 --> 14:31.267
So I guess this is good-bye.

14:31.269 --> 14:32.769
I-I guess so.

14:32.771 --> 14:35.471
Hey, thanks for letting me
crash on your couch

14:35.473 --> 14:36.973
and for the hot shower.

14:36.975 --> 14:39.142
By the way, your staff
is so attentive.

14:39.144 --> 14:41.678
I mean, that Barry kid
checked up on me,

14:41.680 --> 14:44.480
like, five times
during the night.

14:47.885 --> 14:49.719
All right, you know,

14:49.721 --> 14:53.756
I-I don't usually say this
to people in this house, but...

14:53.758 --> 14:56.859
if you want,
you can stay longer.

14:59.063 --> 15:00.997
You're very sweet, Walden,

15:00.999 --> 15:03.066
but, uh, I gotta get going.

15:03.068 --> 15:04.367
Enjoy your view.

15:04.369 --> 15:05.735
(chuckles)

15:08.005 --> 15:09.072
Hey, Vivian.

15:09.074 --> 15:10.073
Yeah?

15:10.075 --> 15:11.541
Are you gonna be okay?

15:11.543 --> 15:13.443
Yeah, I'll be fine.

15:13.445 --> 15:15.545
I mean, this is...
this is what I do.

15:15.547 --> 15:17.480
Okay.

15:18.549 --> 15:20.049
Walden?

15:22.486 --> 15:23.553
Yeah?

15:23.555 --> 15:24.854
Are you gonna be okay?

15:24.856 --> 15:27.790
I do...

15:27.792 --> 15:30.426
think I'm gonna be okay.

15:30.428 --> 15:33.796
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

15:33.798 --> 15:37.900
Okay, I think I, uh,
got all my stuff.

15:37.902 --> 15:39.335
Okay, that is my lamp.

15:39.337 --> 15:42.505
Oh. Oh, yeah, yeah,
but I put a new bulb in it.

15:43.907 --> 15:45.742
So, you know, I'll just wait
till this one blows out,

15:45.744 --> 15:47.076
then I'll shoot it
right back to you.

15:47.078 --> 15:48.811
Okay. Or...

15:55.719 --> 15:57.553
(doorbell rings)

16:01.091 --> 16:03.192
I'll be back for you.

16:05.963 --> 16:07.030
Gretchen?

16:07.032 --> 16:08.231
I'm glad you're here.

16:08.233 --> 16:09.799
I realized the only thing

16:09.801 --> 16:12.502
I actually know about you
is where you live.

16:12.504 --> 16:13.936
Well...

16:13.938 --> 16:16.439
Oh, my God, is everything
about you a lie?

16:16.441 --> 16:17.740
Are you even cheap?

16:17.742 --> 16:19.008
I am cheap.

16:19.010 --> 16:21.677
Two of the four windows
in my car are garbage bags.

16:21.679 --> 16:23.212
Look... look, I know

16:23.214 --> 16:25.314
I was an idiot,
but-but what I said before

16:25.316 --> 16:27.583
about how much I care about you,
I-I meant that.

16:27.585 --> 16:28.751
But... you know,

16:28.753 --> 16:30.953
I-I understand if you want
nothing to do with me.

16:30.955 --> 16:32.255
That's why I'm here.

16:32.257 --> 16:34.524
Look, I made my share
of mistakes

16:34.526 --> 16:35.725
when my husband left me.

16:35.727 --> 16:37.193
I know how hurtful it can be.

16:37.195 --> 16:39.028
I know how crazy you can become.

16:39.030 --> 16:42.665
I mean, I'm sure you Googled me
and saw my mug shots online.

16:42.667 --> 16:45.068
Uh, no. Um...

16:45.070 --> 16:46.669
Well, don't freak out.
I was innocent.

16:46.671 --> 16:49.472
According to the state
of Illinois.

16:49.474 --> 16:51.574
The point is,

16:51.576 --> 16:53.209
we all have secrets.

16:53.211 --> 16:56.245
So, are you saying that we can
get back together?

16:56.247 --> 16:59.682
I'm saying I would like
to break up with Jeff Strongman

16:59.684 --> 17:02.085
and get to know Alan Harper.

17:02.087 --> 17:04.153
Really? Oh, that's great.

17:04.155 --> 17:07.824
But-but first, I'd like
one last moment with Jeff.

17:07.826 --> 17:08.825
Jeff?

17:08.827 --> 17:10.693
Yes?
Screw you.

17:10.695 --> 17:12.328
Oh, God!

17:12.330 --> 17:14.230
(groans)

17:14.232 --> 17:16.632
Oh, are you okay, Alan?

17:19.937 --> 17:21.804
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

17:21.806 --> 17:22.839
Hey, you.

17:22.841 --> 17:25.341
Hey, you're back.

17:25.343 --> 17:29.479
So, I've got good news
and I've got great news.

17:29.481 --> 17:31.647
The good news is,
I did work it out

17:31.649 --> 17:33.216
so I could stay a few more days.

17:33.218 --> 17:35.151
Oh.
And the great news is,

17:35.153 --> 17:37.553
I took my underwear off
in the car.

17:41.558 --> 17:43.526
Hey, um...

17:43.528 --> 17:45.194
(grunts, stammers)

17:46.430 --> 17:49.398
Listen, we need...
we need to talk.

17:49.400 --> 17:51.100
Awfully serious for someone

17:51.102 --> 17:53.569
who just got hit in the face
with a thong.

17:53.571 --> 17:55.872
Here's the thing.

17:57.074 --> 17:59.142
While you were gone,
I met someone.

17:59.144 --> 18:00.776
What?

18:00.778 --> 18:02.879
I mean, nothing happened
physically.

18:02.881 --> 18:06.649
It's just, I can't stop thinking
about her,

18:06.651 --> 18:09.051
and it's made me question
everything,

18:09.053 --> 18:10.486
including my sanity

18:10.488 --> 18:13.156
and my interior
decorating instincts.

18:13.158 --> 18:16.993
Are you saying that you want
to be with this girl now?

18:16.995 --> 18:18.427
I don't know what I want.

18:18.429 --> 18:20.897
I just, I know I have
to pursue this.

18:20.899 --> 18:22.698
Wow.

18:22.700 --> 18:25.201
I'm-I'm-I'm sorry.

18:25.203 --> 18:26.736
I-I never meant to hurt you.

18:26.738 --> 18:28.404
I don't feel the same.

18:28.406 --> 18:30.273
(groans)

18:31.575 --> 18:34.210
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

18:37.014 --> 18:38.114
Hi.

18:38.116 --> 18:39.115
Hi-ya!

18:39.117 --> 18:40.816
(groans)

18:44.588 --> 18:46.022
Oh...

18:46.024 --> 18:48.925
Oh, they had just
dropped back down!

18:48.927 --> 18:51.227
Walden, what are you doing here?

18:51.229 --> 18:53.129
(groans)

18:53.131 --> 18:58.401
Remember how you asked me
if I was gonna be okay?

18:59.136 --> 19:01.270
I don't think I am.

19:01.272 --> 19:03.940
Is it because I just kicked you
in the balls?

19:03.942 --> 19:05.441
There's that.

19:05.443 --> 19:09.979
Uh, but before I met you,

19:09.981 --> 19:13.549
I was very close to asking
another woman to marry me.

19:15.219 --> 19:16.786
But then I didn't...

19:16.788 --> 19:18.387
because I couldn't stop thinking
of you.

19:18.389 --> 19:23.759
So, you came here to tell me
that you dumped your girlfriend,

19:23.761 --> 19:27.463
sweep me off my feet,
and the two of us would,

19:27.465 --> 19:30.600
what, sail off
into the sunset together?

19:34.137 --> 19:35.638
Yes?

19:35.640 --> 19:37.306
You don't even know me.

19:37.308 --> 19:41.410
Okay... I know you enough

19:41.412 --> 19:43.613
to know that I want
to know you more.

19:43.615 --> 19:45.014
Walden, stop it.

19:45.016 --> 19:47.984
I'm just a stranger who wanted
to drink from your hose.

19:49.620 --> 19:51.921
Okay, that didn't... that didn't
really come out right.

19:51.923 --> 19:53.289
Look, I know
I don't know you

19:53.291 --> 19:54.557
very well, but I feel like

19:54.559 --> 19:56.659
you're the type of guy
who falls in love easily.

19:56.661 --> 20:00.029
You know me perfectly!
That's exactly who I am.

20:00.031 --> 20:01.864
I... look, we're soul mates.

20:01.866 --> 20:03.899
Soul mates aren't made in a day.

20:03.901 --> 20:06.836
Oh, that's another
great bumper sticker.

20:06.838 --> 20:09.105
Walden, you're a great guy,

20:09.107 --> 20:11.807
but we lead
two very different lives.

20:11.809 --> 20:13.743
Did I mention
that I have a plane

20:13.745 --> 20:15.945
and I can take you anywhere
you want to go?

20:15.947 --> 20:19.915
Do you see?
You want to fly over everything.

20:19.917 --> 20:22.051
For you, it's all about
the destination.

20:22.053 --> 20:24.820
For me, the journey
is the destination.

20:24.822 --> 20:27.556
Okay, are you writing
these down?

20:29.660 --> 20:31.827
Go home, Walden.

20:34.231 --> 20:36.432
(stammering)

20:36.434 --> 20:38.100
But I-I walked
four miles to get here

20:38.102 --> 20:40.436
in the dark.
In the woods!

20:40.438 --> 20:43.606
I don't even know
if I can find my way home.

20:43.608 --> 20:46.409
Maybe I should just stay
with you.

20:50.380 --> 20:51.881
(alarm chirps)

20:51.883 --> 20:53.382
Ah, dude, there's your car.

20:54.384 --> 20:55.985
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

21:01.842 --> 21:03.343
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

21:03.345 --> 21:04.877
Here you go, sweetie.

21:04.879 --> 21:06.212
Thank you.

21:10.384 --> 21:12.552
I'm so sorry
I freaked out on you.

21:12.554 --> 21:14.153
It's not your fault.

21:14.155 --> 21:16.322
I should've known better.

21:16.324 --> 21:17.990
VIVIAN:
I'm sorry, too.

21:17.992 --> 21:19.959
I should have never let you go.

21:21.695 --> 21:23.529
Well, you're both here now...

21:23.531 --> 21:25.865
and I'm ready to enjoy the view.

21:25.867 --> 21:28.301
You want us to kiss, Walden?

21:28.303 --> 21:31.304
Yeah, kiss each other.

21:34.641 --> 21:35.708
&lt;i>Do it.&lt;/i>

21:35.710 --> 21:37.543
Kiss each other.

21:39.885 --> 21:41.419
Well, it is his house.

21:41.421 --> 21:46.421
